# Case review — state preservation bug (Steve)

**Status:** Documented — do NOT implement yet. Steve is studying.

## Symptom
After placing all orders and completing the review (or watching the teaching video), returning to the case shows no pins/stacks — everything is gone.

## Root cause
`Play.jsx` → `completeNow` (line ~3085-3107) calls:
- `clearPlayCheckpoint()` — wipes active checkpoint
- `clearCasePlayCheckpoint(caseData.id)` — wipes saved case snapshot
- `onComplete(result)` — navigates away

The checkpoint that held `placed`, `pins`, and `placementOrder` is deleted. On re-entry, `resumePlaySession` finds no checkpoint and the case starts fresh.

## Why this is wrong
The user's stacks represent their clinical reasoning. After review, the learner should still see their work — what they ordered, where they placed it, what was correct/missed. The review panel shows this, but once exited, it's gone.

## Expected behavior
- After completing review: stacks remain visible on the patient (with ok/bad markings from review)
- Placements persist across case re-entries
- The checkpoint should NOT be cleared — instead, mark it as "completed" so pins/placed are still loaded
- Or: save a separate "completed snapshot" that the case always loads as the "last attempt display"

## Files involved
- `src/components/Play.jsx` — `completeNow`, `wrapUpCase`, `confirmExitCase`
- `src/lib/playCheckpoint.js` — `clearPlayCheckpoint`, `clearCasePlayCheckpoint`

